  back={{ href: '/apps/below', label: 'Below' }}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> Below shrinks your files entirely on your device. Your videos, photos and PDFs are never uploaded. There is no account, and Below does not collect, transmit, or share your information. On iPhone and iPad, Below downloads a small public list of size limits from our website once a day; that request carries no information about you.
  </div>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>None.</strong> Below does not require an account, does not ask you to sign in, and does not collect personal information or other user data.</p>

  <h2>Your Videos, Photos and PDFs</h2>
  <p>
    Every file Below reads and every file Below writes stays on your device. Videos are compressed with the video framework built into iOS or Android, and photos and PDFs (iPhone and iPad only) with the image and PDF frameworks built into iOS. Below performs no upload, so your files are never sent to us or to anyone else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Below never modifies or deletes your original. It writes a new, smaller copy. When Below makes a photo copy, it leaves out the location, camera details and other personal information stored in the original. This happens on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Size-Limit List</h2>
  <p>
    On iPhone and iPad, Below version 2.0 and later keeps an up-to-date list of common upload and attachment limits (for example, Discord or Gmail). At most once a day it downloads that list, a public file, from <code>mattdonders.com</code>. The request includes no account, device identifier, advertising identifier, file information, or anything you have done in the app. As with any web request, our hosting provider (Cloudflare) sees the network address the request comes from; we do not use it to identify you or for anything else. If the download fails, Below uses the list built into the app. The Android app does not download this list.
  </p>
  <h2>Tracking, Analytics, and Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Below does not use analytics, crash-reporting services, advertising, tracking, third-party SDKs, or third-party services. It does not track you across apps or websites. Because Below does not collect your information, it does not sell or share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Below Pro is a one-time in-app purchase processed by Apple through the App Store on iPhone and iPad, or by Google through Google Play on Android. The store handles the transaction and tells Below only whether the purchase is active. We do not receive your payment details or any other personal information from that transaction. Each store's handling of purchase data is covered by its own privacy policy (Apple's or Google's).
  </p>

  <h2>Device Access and Data Management</h2>
  <p>
    Below asks for permission to add a video or photo to your photo library only when you choose to save a result. Choosing a file through the system photo picker or the system file picker requires no permission, because those pickers hand Below only the single item you select.
  </p>
  <p>
    Below stores a small amount of information on your device: the sizes you save for reuse, a count of how many free uses you have used, whether Below Pro is unlocked, and the most recent size-limit list. That information is shared only between Below, its share extension, and its Shortcuts action on the same device. You can remove it by deleting the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Below is not directed at children and collects no information from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>Any future changes to this policy will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Below%20Privacy">matt@mattdonders.com</a>.</p>
